{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Allow People with Mild, Well-Controlled Asthma to Join the UK Armed Forces",
        "additional_details": "Many people with mild asthma are fit, healthy and capable of serving in the Armed Forces, but are still turned away because of their condition.\r\n\r\nHaving asthma shouldn't automatically stop someone from following their dream of joining the military. People with mild, well-controlled asthma should have the chance to prove they are fit enough through proper medical checks and fitness tests.\r\n\r\nEveryone deserves a fair chance to serve their country, as long as they can do so safely.",
        "background": "Allow people with mild, well-controlled asthma to join the British Armed Forces. We want the Government to change the current medical entry requirements so applicants are assessed on their individual health, fitness and ability to serve safely, rather than being rejected due to mild asthma.",
